  "body": "## Context\n12th offered to merge the features from my Little Zen version, except its one-line installer. This PR ports the remaining runtime and interface differences into the upstream mod. Features already present upstream stay in place.\n\n## Included\n- Keep links, searches, and container-extension redirects in Little Zen; do not apply Zen Space routing to its startup URL.\n- Preserve the main Zen window's navbar and prevent Ctrl+Alt+tab click from also opening split view.\n- Keep pinned extension buttons beside the sidebar URL bar until it is full, and use readable fallback colors on pages without theme colors.\n- Size a compact Little Zen window to its URL bar, place the Space picker in the right-side toolbar spring, and align the toolbar and frame CSS with my version.\n- Keep upstream's startup presentation helper while retaining the same user-facing behavior.\n\nThe non-Sine installation, one-line installer, and bundled fx-autoconfig files are intentionally excluded. Upstream's Sine mod packaging remains unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n- `node --check littleZen.uc.js`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `chrome.css` matches the CSS from my repo byte-for-byte.\n- The pinned-extension flow was confirmed in my local Zen profile with the corresponding fork code. This upstream branch has not been installed separately for a UI check.",
